    "q-36824": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36824",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3-\\lambda  \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3)+2(2\\lambda -2)-3(2\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda )+(4\\lambda -4)-(6\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
