    "q-86753": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86753",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,R-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nR-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(R-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st column, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -4)+2(-2\\lambda +7) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -4)+(-4\\lambda +14) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
